WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Ganju Station / Nanjo City

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Tourism Information Center

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.230
Kudaka-san,
Nanjo General Clinic is on line two.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.110
Okay.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.360
Thanks for your call, Kudaka here.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.770
I'm in your care.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.350
Really?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.110
Huh?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.990
Really? We can do that?

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.300
A traveling aquarium?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:18.830
Yeah.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.400
I just got a call
from the person in charge.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.710
We officially have permission.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.240
Nice!

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.940
A traveling aquarium?

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:33.220
We take marine life on tour for people
who can't make it to the aquarium.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.140
We'll be doing it at the pediatrics
department of Nanjo General Clinic.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.670
Huh.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.400
Oh, yeah, we need to tell Umi-yan.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.480
This was his idea, after all.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.640
Really?!

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.980
Karin-chan, thank you so much!

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.530
Oh, but there's one condition on us
doing the traveling aquarium.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.130
A condition?

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.610
Take this too, please.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.160
There we go.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.000
Huh?

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.630
That's it?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.560
Didn't we bring more species along before?

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.470
Where are the crabs?

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:38.510
No, no, no!

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.180
Crabs are banned.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:42.090
Banned?

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.930
The pediatrics head nurse said...

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.940
I'm really scared of the C-word.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.100
"C"?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.210
They have two pincers, and they crawl
side to side with their eight legs.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.190
Those things give me the chills.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.490
Oh, you mean crabs.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.280
Stop!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.920
Don't even say the word!

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.820
What a hideous name.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.910
Do <i>not</i> bring them.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.320
Can you promise that?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.680
She hates crabs <i>that</i> much?

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.790
Does she have some kind
of beef with them?

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.930
Let's take these guys, too.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.510
Garra rufa?

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:24.990
Correct.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.650
They're going to be our stars today.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.230
I'm sure they'll be popular.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.810
Want a ride next to me, Fuuka-chan?

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.860
Want the AC?

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.700
Okay, I'll see you there.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.520
Too bad for you.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.060
These'll keep you company.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.460
They're way better than her.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.340
Hey, riding with you
won't be bad, either.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.540
All right, we're counting on you!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.980
Nanjo General Clinic

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.820
Admission Card

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:24.820
Here you go.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.000
Thanks.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:26.820
Here.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.830
Thank you.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.800
The venue is in the general
purpose room on the third floor.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.750
We start at 1 P.M., after lunchtime.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.210
You can bring in supplies from there.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:39.210
Be sure not to disturb the patients.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.320
Yeah, okay.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.220
You're kind of amazing.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.150
You're so on-the-ball.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.630
Karin-chan's a capable woman.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.970
Hey! No toying with grown-ups.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.320
We don't have time.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.160
Hurry.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.190
Okay.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:00.590
I'll take care of carrying the equipment.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.200
Take care of these kids for me.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.630
It'll get too warm outside, huh?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.380
Yeah.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.700
Let's bring them in quickly.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.080
Is your back okay, though?

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.670
No problem.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.920
I've been working on my muscles.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.840
Are you sure you're okay?

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.340
No problem...

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:32.560
Is this it?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.830
Seems so.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.390
Sorry we left it so cluttered here.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.670
Kinjou-san.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.300
Good morning!

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:45.660
I wanted to make sure you'd have plenty
of space, but we didn't have enough staff.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.480
We'll take care of it. It's all right.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.650
Oh, there's something I wanted to give you!

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.560
I'm sorry. I'm in a hurry right now.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.000
I'll be back later.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.670
I brought the stuff.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.590
I had a creepy feeling just now.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:11.890
Head Nurse!

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.770
I'll be right there.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.200
So heavy.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.840
I'll take it.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:28.060
Fuuka-chan, do you happen
to be pretty strong?

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.240
I think I got stronger
from working at Gama Gama.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:38.240
People tend to think we just sit there
looking pretty at aquariums,

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.750
but there's quite a bit of heavy-lifting.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.510
Wow.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.630
I'll leave the tank here.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.830
Okay.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.440
Let's tidy up quickly.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.270
Do you always lay down a tarp?

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.500
We absolutely don't want
to make a mess at the venue.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.790
We don't want to let a single drop
of water get on the floor.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.010
Huh.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.010
Is the aquarium here?

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.000
After lunch.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.190
We brought fish and starfish and stuff.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.280
You should come check it out.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.200
Okay!

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.160
She's not here.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.310
What is it?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.630
Oh, nothing.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.880
I'm going to go get some things
that I left behind.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.120
Kudaka here.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:34.220
Yes.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.470
Understood.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.720
Kukuru, Kinjou-san has some time now.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.000
Fuuka, can you take care
of the rest by yourself?

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.480
Leave it to me.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.150
I'll get the prep done.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:46.860
Thanks.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.550
Okay, I'll see you later.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.400
Crab!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.560
How?

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.070
No one's looking, are they?

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.120
What do I do?

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.180
Um...

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.420
A bucket!

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.980
Ow!

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.940
Is something the matter?

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.190
There is no matter!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.310
I-I see.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:37.850
No way!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.040
Let's see...

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.760
Um...

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.230
Where is Uehara-san?

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.470
Airi-chan is in Room 306.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.220
306 South

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.220
Uehara Airi

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.220
Otonohara Miki

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.220
Miyasato Juri

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.130
Hey, long time, no...

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.270
Thanks for being so considerate.

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:13.820
For the children.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.570
I'm sure they'll be ecstatic.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.180
Do you like garden eels?

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.700
They're so adorable, huh?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.840
Their faces are so expressive!

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.120
They look around for food
with their huge eyes!

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.330
And when food drifts along,
they stretch out to catch it.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:37.900
Sometimes they catch something else
by accident and puke it out.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.390
Kukuru.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:44.350
You really love fish,
don't you, Misakino-san?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.810
She goes off into her own world
when it comes to fish.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.600
You're quite the passionate person
as well, Kudaka-san.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:52.610
Me?

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:57.080
I heard from PR that you've submitted
event proposals several times

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.110
to try to make the
traveling aquarium happen.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.720
Karin-chan...

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.560
Oh, it's nothing.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.870
They said they were moved by your desire

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.010
to make it come to life
before the aquarium closed.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.820
Everyone's looking forward to it.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.880
We'll be in your care today.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:17.680
So will we.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.270
I look forward to working with you.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.220
Kukuru.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.770
Anyone would expect that we're closing.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:35.240
I've been going to Gama Gama
since I was a kid.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:37.080
I have a lot of memories there.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.550
I really don't want it to close, either!

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:45.410
But no matter how many times I talk
to the city, I don't get a positive response.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.120
There's nothing we can do at this rate.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:53.480
Working at the Tourism Association,
I get all sorts of information.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:57.420
There's a lot of enthusiasm for the aquarium
that's being built at the center.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:02.300
Even if Gama Gama survives,
the tourists will...

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.000
It's not here.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.580
I can't find it anywhere.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.710
What do I do?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.570
Umi-yan!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.820
Help me!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:21.100
Crab!

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:32.630
Are we missing one?

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:35.260
Is it just my imagination?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.430
No, but...

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.880
Maybe you're tired.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:40.920
No kidding.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.260
I did three people's worth of work.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.550
Kukuru and the others are working hard
right about now, too.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.310
What's the matter?

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:03.950
Gama Gama...

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.950
Do you think it's going to close, too?

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.660
I don't know.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:18.570
Nothing about the future
is ever certain.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.650
We can only do the best we can
for the time now.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.680
Is that why you came up
with the traveling aquarium?

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.220
That's right.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.720
But I don't know
if this was the right decision.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.220
What do you mean?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.800
You know Airi-chan, the girl who used
to come to Gama Gama often?

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:39.290
Oh, the girl that had lots
of requests for you.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.060
Yeah.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.490
That girl's hospitalized here.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.810
I made her a promise before.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.680
It's still not here!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.500
You promised you'd have garra rufa.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.040
You liar!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.350
Sorry, sorry.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.230
Next week.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.260
The tests will be done next week,
and then we can put them on display.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:05.990
Promise?

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:07.630
Promise.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.500
I'll have them here
for sure this time.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:10.760
You'd better look forward to it.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.700
Okay.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.750
I get to see them next week.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:15.740
Yay!

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.270
Thanks, Umi-yan.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:23.560
But Airi-chan stopped coming the next week.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.500
She didn't come the week after that,
or the week after.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:30.660
And I ended up taking a break
to deal with my back pain.

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:37.040
And then, the other day, I heard from
Rui-kun that she's hospitalized here.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.460
I see.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.540
That's why...

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.190
Shoot!

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.490
A xanthid crab came along!

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.800
Let's get back!

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:53.820
What do we do? We don't have time.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:57.210
We've looked really hard,
and we still can't find it, which means...

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.310
Was I mistaken?

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:02.460
No, it definitely pinched me.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:03.530
Sorry, I'm here now!

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.780
Oh, man!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.950
You're almost done.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.280
Sorry to make you do all the work.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.360
So, is it true that a xanthid crab—

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.290
Seems that you're all set.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.120
It's a bit early,
but shall we get started?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:23.050
The children are really eager.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.460
R-Right.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.640
I'll sneak out to look for them.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.550
Take care of the kids for me.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.120
Welcome

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.120
Gama Gama

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.120
Traveling

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.120
Aquarium

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.470
Whoa, it kinda stinks.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.590
It smells like the sea.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:40.320
I'm touching this?

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.840
Touch it gently in the water.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.110
It's cold.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.960
It feels rough.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.110
Weird!

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.900
This one's a sand dollar.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:53.520
It's going to burrow into the sand.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.030
Watch carefully.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:06.880
That's so weird.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:09.260
Hey, what's this one?

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.240
That one's called a cushion star.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.600
It's round like a steamed bun, right?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.680
It looks nasty!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.230
Wash your hands
when you're done looking.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.560
Okay!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.800
Well? It tickles, doesn't it?

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.580
Airi-chan!

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:39.540
Wait.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.500
Come look and touch them.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:50.490
You've been wanting
to see them so much.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.980
It's not the same.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.600
It's not the same anymore.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.770
The animals of the sea don't mind.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.400
I don't care to see them.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.880
I don't like fish at all!

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:07.650
I don't want to see them!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.780
Go away!

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.780
Give me a second.

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:17.780
What's the matter?

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:23.880
Shall we go back to your room?

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.860
Help me...

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:04.540
Kinjou-san!

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.370
Wait.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.860
Are you all right?

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:32.040
Let's go rest over there.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.110
I'll take you.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:36.340
It's alive.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.720
Thank you.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:42.500
Let's go.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:48.250
Here.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.340
Garra rufa are also called doctor fish.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:15.970
They eat dead skin cells,
so they make your skin healthy.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:17.280
That's my girl.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.120
Thanks, Umi-yan.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:25.510
Yup.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.130
A new promise?

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:36.480
As long as you aren't going to ask
for whales or dolphins or anything.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.350
No, I'm going to make a promise.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:46.930
I'm going to be strong, so I can
go back to Gama Gama someday.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.540
Yeah.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.590
Promise.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.220
Gama Gama is...

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.420
I'm so sorry.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:09.290
I can't believe we brought a crab—
I mean, a C-word along.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.670
We're truly sorry.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:17.420
I can't let this slide, especially
from a hygiene standpoint.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:21.800
I'll be filing a formal complaint with
the aquarium and Tourism Association...

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.660
...is what I'm tempted to say.

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:30.670
But in consideration of the smiles
you've brought to the children's faces,

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:33.060
I'll look the other way, just this once.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:37.190
I've never seen their eyes
sparkle so much here.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:42.320
It's thanks to you all and the... crab.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:53.960
Karin-chan.

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:57.320
Sorry about earlier.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:01.220
I came off really nasty.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:05.220
Nah.

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:11.940
Hey, I like aquarium attendants.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.440
Have I ever told you my dream?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.860
I wanted to be an aquarium attendant.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:20.920
Really?

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.440
I was pretty serious about it, too.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:32.140
But my parents were struggling
with their business.

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:36.210
So they talked me into
finding a stable job.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:41.210
I could see where my parents
were coming from, so that's what I did.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:46.380
This job's fun,
and it feels really worthwhile.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:50.640
But I noticed that ever since the day
I gave up on becoming an aquarium attendant,

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:55.880
I got better at forcing myself
to accept things.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:02.860
So when I see you going headlong
toward your dream, I get really envious.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:05.220
You're strong.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:11.820
I'm not strong.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:18.260
It's just that if I give up,
Gama Gama is finished.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.780
So...

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.470
I won't ever give up!

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:30.800
Hey!

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:32.980
Let's go home.

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.310
"Won't give up," huh?

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:29.470
I'm here from Aquarium Tingaara for training.

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:31.290
My name is Haebaru Chiyu.

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:32.980
I'll be in your care.
